+## Descent sources
+
+The Stacks Project, Proposition 35.5.2, Tag 023T, states effectivity and full faithfulness of fpqc descent for quasi-coherent modules. Section 35.6, Tag 0CDQ, describes the Galois double overlap. The article supplies its invariant ideal, equivariant inclusion, cocycle, and base-change-exact intersection diagram before applying these results.
+
+- https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/023T
+- https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CDQ
+- https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AS
+
+The Cauchy/Schur framework is attributed to the inherited Fulton--Harris and De Concini--Eisenbud--Procesi references. The two-component extraction, global ruling orientation, and separating witnesses are proved in the article, with finite identities independently recomputed.
+
